# Report on dump

**Feature name (owner):** **Report on dump**

When the owner says **Report on dump**, **dump report**, **update diff**, **vX.Y changelog from MasterData**, or hands you a dump/HTML diff after a client import — do a **deep dive**. List **all** meaningful diffs clearly. Explain every player-facing term in **EN + TW/HK in-game LANG** (not free translation).

Typical inputs: `Desktop/dump/dump*.cs`, `Diff Report - dumpA vs dumpB.html`, current `ggen_db_app/data/{EN,TW,HK}/{master,lang}/`.  
Default output: `Desktop/dump/` bilingual markdown — **two files**:

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `GGEN_Detail_Report_dump…_EN_TW.md` | **Full** deep dive — Enums, MemoryTables, schema fields, TypeIndex, counts, MD status, LANG cites |
| `GGEN_Not_Live_Yet_Features_dump…_EN_TW.md` | **Short share note only** — community bullets; no Enum/MT soup |

## Hard rule — Detail vs Not-live (owner — Nov 2026 / 2.8)

1. **All technical detail stays on the Detail report** — every MemoryTable / Enum / schema field / TypeIndex / row count / LIVE·PARTIAL·SCAFFOLD·CLIENT ONLY / file+field cite. Do **not** thin the Detail report to match the share note.
2. **Not-live companion = shareable TW/EN bullets** — short player-facing list (Unit Skills, IR conditions, Story Event Challenge Battle, victory conditions, “already in client”). Match the owner’s preferred shape (see 2.8 lesson). **No** enum names, MT keys, or schema tables in Not-live unless the owner asks.
3. Do **not** rewrite Not-live into a second Detail report. If something needs Enums/MTs, it goes in Detail (or a one-line pointer to Detail).

## Hard rule — Detail report content

1. **Write for reading** — prefer a community-note shape for *headings and lead insights*, but keep full technical annexes:
   - Lead with **insights the owner would not already have** (mission condition enums, swap tables, dual SSP/Ult channels, Style product, battle-power on buffs, …) — not a restatement of a six-bullet community note
   - New effects / skills (numbered list)
   - New fields on traits / conditions / Unit Skills (what each enables)
   - Big systems (ULT改造, events, Profile, …)
   - Then MD status (LIVE / PARTIAL / SCAFFOLD / CLIENT ONLY)
   - Section titles must be **plain language**. Never opaque labels like “A6 Schema”.
2. **Actually deep-dive the dump** — parse MemoryTable + Enum diffs (`_mt_diff_key` / `_enum_diff_key` / HTML / CS). Cross-check live `data/*/master` row usage. Surface **every** new `GameEventConditionType`, function/payload enum, user table, and schema field — not only headline features. If the report only repeats what a short community list already said, it failed.
3. **List all diffs** — not only flashy items. Include new/removed tables, schema fields (even if all default), new enums/TypeIndex with counts, new content rows, LANG-only changes when relevant.
4. **Do not omit scaffolds** — column exists but unused → still report, say unused / no content yet, and what it is *for* when inferable from sibling live content (e.g. `TargetWeaponConditionId` + max-range Unit Skill ≈ “Beam／光束／鐳射 weapons max range +1”).
5. **Combat correction shape (mandatory for new TraitTypes)** — open `TraitCorrection*` / `*CalculateService` in the dump CS. Count **how many numbers** the correction stores, merge/highest helpers, and whether values read from the **unit** (skills／abilities can stack) vs weapon-only. Example: Splash = **Rate + Range** (`TraitCorrectionSplashDamage`), `_SelectHighestSplashDamage`, `GetSplashDamageRange(attacker)` → skills/abilities can expand **Range** later. Put the player-facing dual numbers in **both** Detail and Not-live — never flatten to “Splash added.” Pair new `TraitValue2` / dual MD columns with what the second number **is**.
6. **Substance over labels** — empty one-liners (“Profile 2.0 — partial”) are not enough. For Profile / systems: list real table counts, LANG examples (ranks, records, titles, styles), and what is still blocked.
7. **Bilingual — in-game LANG only**
   - EN: `data/EN/lang/` · Trad Chinese: prefer **TW**; note **HK** when different (Beam→鐳射)
   - Start with a **LANG glossary** for terms used in that report
   - No fan translations. Missing mode/item **title** → keep client EN + mark **`LANG missing` / `LANG 未進包`**
   - Traps: Chance Step→**額外行動** (not CS); Preemptive Strike→**先發攻擊** (not 先制); Skip Great Success→**超成功**; Ult Custom→**ULT改造**; Profile→**簡介**; Style→**風格**; Stage Skip→**略過關卡**; Tags→**標籤**; weapon attributes→**武裝屬性**; damage noun→**損傷**
8. **LANG missing ≠ omit the feature** — many client diffs are not in the live update / LANG pack yet. Still **list them in full**. Explain with **in-game LANG vocabulary** already used elsewhere (e.g. **故事事件**, **增幅**, **編制**, **標籤**, **系列**, **單位技能**, **損傷**, **額外行動**, **簡介**). Pattern:
   - Keep client EN name as the temporary title (`Invasion Restriction`, …) + `LANG 未進包`
   - Body: describe flow/effects using existing help/trait words in **EN | TW/HK**
   - Never drop a whole system because its menu title string is absent
9. Cite **file + field** (`m_trait.RangeMin`, `m_trait_condition.IsHpDamaged`, `m_unit_skill_trait.TargetWeaponConditionId`, …).
10. Pair Detail with a **Not live yet** companion when client ships systems without MD / with scaffolds only.
11. **Do not put website-only bugs in Report on dump** (e.g. UI inventing a Tag from a field). Fix the site separately; the dump report stays MasterData / client content.

## Anti-patterns

- Only “6 new abilities” without the new trait/condition/Unit Skill fields
- Restating a short community list with nicer formatting and calling it a deep dive
- Putting Enums / MemoryTables / schema tables into the **Not-live** share file
- Thinning the **Detail** report so Enums/MTs only appear in Not-live (or nowhere)
- EN-only report
- Free-translated TW/HK
- Calling scaffolds “not in the dump”
- **Skipping** Invasion / Field Story / Buff systems (or similar) just because the **title** has no LANG yet
- One-liner stubs for LANG-pending features (“client only, title pending”) with no player-facing explanation
- Section titles nobody can parse (“Schema”, “A6b”, internal enum soup as the only heading)
- Padding the dump report with site-bug writeups
- Flattening dual-value combat systems to a single label (e.g. “Splash added” without **Rate + Range**, merge/highest, skill/ability expand path)

## Lessons

### v2.8 Splash Rate + Range (owner — Nov 2026)

**Proven:** Splash combat correction is **Rate + Range** (`TraitCorrectionSplashDamage`); build param has `TraitValue`+`TraitValue2`; `_SelectHighestSplashDamage`; `GetSplashDamageRange(attacker)`. MD `TraitValue2` still all 0. Grant pipelines onto `TraitType`: weapon **GrantTrait** / ability **TraitSet**.

**Not proven:** “skills/abilities expand Splash Range.” In Not-live say **not confirmed**／**尚未確認** — simple, direct; no “client,” “our guess,” or GrantTrait jargon. Detail may keep grant-path evidence.

**Must appear in Detail + Not-live:** Rate+Range; honest grant-path wording — not only “範圍損傷／map preview.”

### v2.8 Not-live share shape (owner — Nov 2026)

Owner’s preferred Not-live bullets (keep this class; Detail still holds all Enums/MTs). Prefer community code-analysis polish (Grok/EN+繁中 share tone) when wording Splash / Skip / Unit Skills:

- 新增單位技能 — **爆擊提升**（Critical Boost）/ **確定爆擊**（Guaranteed Critical）— LANG **爆擊** not 暴擊
- 武裝新增 Splash — 周邊數格**衰減損傷**；弱化擴散周邊；**Rate＋Range** 分開、多筆取最高；「技能／能力擴大範圍」標 **尚未確認／not confirmed**（簡寫，勿寫 client／our guess／GrantTrait 術語）
- 戰役／活動 **略過次數繰越**（Skip Stock）— 各關卡未使用略過可繰越至隔天之後（LANG **略過** not 跳過）
- 地圖活動改修 — 夥伴滿解可替換能力
- 下次特務模式限制 — 指定角色標籤／系列
- 故事事件挑戰戰鬥 — N、H、EX、Hell、Inferno
- 勝利條件 — 最後才擊敗敵人
- 其餘已在客戶端 — 活動開放獎勵、簡介任務、單位搜尋篩選強化

Detail keeps the honest grant-path note (UnitSkillTraitType has no Splash; skill Range-up = **not confirmed**).

### v2.7 (owner)

Must include, beyond six Unit Skill types:

- Trait **range** → `m_trait.RangeMin` / `RangeMax`
- Condition **unit damaged** → `m_trait_condition.IsHpDamaged`
- Unit Skill **target weapon** → `TargetWeaponConditionId` (+ link to max-range / Beam·光束·鐳射 wording already live on normal traits)

### Profile

“Profile partial” needs the actual **簡介** pieces: ranks, achievement tiers, user/cumulative records, titles, Style tips — and what LANG/MD is still missing — not a one-line stub.

## Diff_auto / MasterData folder diffs (owner — Oct 2026)

When the owner points at `GGen_Database/Diff_auto(…)/index.html` (or “latest update diff” / MasterData_A → MasterData_B):

1. **Resolve every opaque id to player-facing content** — do not stop at “new schedule Id=…”.
2. For each changed row, **cross-search the newer MasterData tree** for that id (`ScheduleId`, `GashaId`, `ItemId`, `RewardSetId`, `EventId`, `ItemTypeIndex`, gift message id, etc.) and name what it belongs to (LANG EN; TW/HK when quoting UI).
3. **ItemTypeIndex / enum-only rows** — expand to the enum name **and** list concrete items (or “whole class: N tickets”) so it’s clear what players see.
4. **Orphan ids** — if nothing in client master references a new `m_schedule` / reward / gift id, say so explicitly (`no client cross-ref; likely server present / reserved`). Still show JST start/end.
5. Same patch: **wire gift + reward + schedule together** when ids share a date pattern or appear together (maintenance apology gift, etc.).
